Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Diachronic Word Embeddings", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"bfc13d9d-f9c4-4349-b017-7466035b5295"],

Cell["\<\
200 Years of Semantic Drift, Traced Through a Word-Embedding Space\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"6d4747f2-dc7d-497a-adc2-6766396a0a55"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Word meanings move. ",
 StyleBox["Gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " once meant carefree; ",
 StyleBox["broadcast",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " meant to scatter seed by hand; a ",
 StyleBox["computer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " was a person who did arithmetic. This notebook makes that motion visible. ",
 "Using the HistWords decade-by-decade embeddings (word2vec / SGNS trained on \
",
 "the Google N-grams English corpus, one model per decade from the 1800s to \
the ",
 "1990s), we bring two centuries of independently-trained embedding spaces \
into a ",
 "single comparable frame with ",
 StyleBox["orthogonal Procrustes alignment",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", then trace individual words as ",
 StyleBox["trajectories",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " through a 2-D projection of that shared space. The paths \[Dash] a word \
drifting ",
 "past the neighbours that anchor each era of its meaning \[Dash] are the \
point of the ",
 "project. We close by recovering, from the same data, the two ",
 StyleBox["statistical laws of semantic change",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " of Hamilton, Leskovec & Jurafsky (2016). ",
 "Everything here is computed in the Wolfram Language."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 10}},
 FontSize->14,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.96, 0.97, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"b88193f5-0d82-416b-83fd-7317e77acb44"],

