 ShowCellLabel->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"c06d5464-232b-481e-81b0-d379bc92eb5b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Figure. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Six words, two centuries. Each panel projects one word's decade ",
 "vectors (blue = 1800s \[Rule] red = 1990s) into a 2-D map of its own \
changing ",
 "neighbourhood. The animated version (",
 StyleBox["docs/images/hero.gif",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ") draws each path on decade at a time."
}], "Caption",
 CellMargins->{{55, 55}, {2, 
  16}},ExpressionUUID->"04987608-835d-4fcf-9896-d09d40388eef"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. The idea: words as moving points", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"970b5a67-ae47-4a00-9b40-3c5ef6b681d3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A word embedding places every word at a point in a high-dimensional ",
 "space so that words used in similar contexts sit close together. Train one ",
 "embedding on text from the 1850s and another on text from the 1990s and you \
get ",
 "two maps of the language \[Dash] and a word that has changed its meaning \
will sit ",
 "in a different neighbourhood on the two maps. ",
 StyleBox["Gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " sits among ",
 StyleBox["cheerful, merry, lively",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " on the 1850s map and among ",
 StyleBox["homosexual, lesbian, bisexual",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " on the 1990s map. If we can line the maps ",
 "up, we can draw the move as an arrow \[Dash] and across twenty decades, as \
a path."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"25e72477-25e4-4587-8d05-86689ec2a7d4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. The data: HistWords decade embeddings", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0f0bd6a8-037e-4d42-87e5-2fc1939cc67b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We use the ",
 StyleBox["HistWords",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " embeddings of Hamilton et al.: ",
 "300-dimensional skip-gram-with-negative-sampling (SGNS) vectors, trained ",
 "separately for each decade on the Google N-grams ",
 StyleBox["eng-all",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " corpus, ",
 "covering the 1800s through the 1990s \[Dash] twenty decade-models, each \
with a ",
 "100,000-word vocabulary. The vectors are L2-normalized; words absent from a \
",
 "decade are stored as zero vectors and skipped. The raw download is ~1.6 GB \
and ",
 "is not committed; a thin Python shim converts the NumPy/pickle files to \
plain ",
 "float32 binaries, and all of the analysis below is Wolfram Language."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"4030a61d-f198-4bd4-b5e0-c9b8f13a3825"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Of the six headline words, ",
 StyleBox["gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["awful",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["literally",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " appear in all twenty decades; ",
 StyleBox["queer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " from the 1830s, ",
 StyleBox["broadcast",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " from the 1850s, and ",
 StyleBox["computer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " at 1900 (the human-\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]computer\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
sense) ",
 "then continuously from the 1940s (the machine)."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"e17cd732-b925-4b68-b4dc-0b83a48fec08"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Why the decades must be aligned", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"08dca50d-762f-4127-87b7-0864a876001e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each decade's embedding is trained independently, so its coordinate ",
 "axes are arbitrary: the two maps can be rotated and reflected relative to \
one ",
 "another even when they agree perfectly about which words are near which. \
Before ",
 "any word can be tracked through time, the decades must be rotated into a \
common ",
 "frame. We use ",
 StyleBox["orthogonal Procrustes alignment",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ": for the matrices ",
 StyleBox["A",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (a decade) and ",
 StyleBox["B",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (the 1990s reference) holding the vectors of the 5,000 highest-frequency \
words ",
 "present in every decade, we seek the orthogonal ",
 StyleBox["R",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " minimising"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"e5ac3474-6dd0-42cf-bd9c-08fe3fc749cf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["argmin", 
    StyleBox["R",
     FontSlant->Italic]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
    "\[LeftDoubleBracketingBar]", "A", " ", "R", " ", "-", " ", "B", 
     "\[RightDoubleBracketingBar]"}], "2"], " ", 
   RowBox[{"with", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["R", "T"], "R", "=", "I"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellMargins->{{80, 50}, {8, 
  8}},ExpressionUUID->"46bd0737-ca18-4379-9432-73618cd554bf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "whose closed-form solution is ",
 StyleBox["R",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " = ",
 StyleBox["U",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " ",
 StyleBox["V",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "T",
 " from the singular value decomposition ",
 StyleBox["U S V",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "T",
 " = ",
 StyleBox["A",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "T",
 " ",
 StyleBox["B",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ". Because ",
 StyleBox["R",
  FontSlant->Italic]
}], " is orthogonal it preserves all within-", "decade distances \[Dash] it \
only reorients the space \[Dash] so nearest neighbours \
",ExpressionUUID->"47492a3d-015e-461e-b7db-842f0ca66bb0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"stay", " ", "exactly", " ", "as", " ", "trained"}], ",", " ", 
  RowBox[{"while", " ", "becoming", " ", "comparable", " ", "across", " ", 
   RowBox[{"decades", "."}]}]}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7517b0ff-29b2-4c0e-\
93c1-3b7b1cf4b878"],

Cell[BoxData["Text"], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b2acb7a7-1375-4e5e-a5d5-5edd3079964d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 CellMargins -> {{50, 50}, {6, 6}}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7df451a3-7d86-454d-92d7-f3edf2821b67"],

Cell["\<\
This step is necessary, not cosmetic. The rotations are large (the 1800s map \
is rotated by nearly the maximum possible amount onto the 1990s map), and \
alignment measurably raises the cross-decade cosine similarity of stable \
words (e.g. the average for the 5,000 anchor words rises from 0.50 to 0.65 \
between the 1900s and the 1990s).\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"cb030337-3934-433f-abf1-daf778ec8b23"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. Reading a trajectory: six words, six stories", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d16464f9-d6fe-465f-8ed0-e5a4fc56251a"],

Cell["\<\
For each word we collect its aligned vector in every decade in which it \
occurs, gather the nearest neighbours that anchor each era, and project the \
whole local neighbourhood to two dimensions with PCA. The word's path threads \
between an early-meaning cluster and a late-meaning cluster; the colour runs \
blue (1800s) to red (1990s), and dashed segments mark gaps in coverage.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"256524a0-ee45-4161-b038-5cac5ec65b70"],

