}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["7. Two statistical laws of semantic change", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b422f625-98eb-4766-9996-75894ee12d3e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Hamilton, Leskovec & Jurafsky (2016) report two regularities that hold ",
 "across languages and corpora. Both fall out of the same aligned embeddings, \
",
 "measured over the ~8,800 dictionary content words present in every decade \
",
 "(function words and archaic/foreign tokens removed via a stoplist and \
WordNet ",
 "membership). A word's ",
 StyleBox["rate of change",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " is the mean cosine distance ",
 "between its aligned vectors in consecutive decades."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"69284ff7-cb4b-4001-9b99-903c7bf344ac"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The law of conformity", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"4b8b01e5-09cd-4a32-bce7-eec08002fcce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Frequent words change more slowly.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Plotting the log rate of ",
 "change against a frequency proxy (negative log mean rank) gives a negative \
slope ",
 "(\[TildeTilde] \[Minus]0.05, Pearson r \[TildeTilde] \[Minus]0.21): the \
more ",
 "common a word, the more anchored its meaning."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"d597209c-f4fa-419d-a6d2-e64dae339c32"],

